Week 11 was system integration week and the most revealing in terms of environment-specific bugs. The spike alert failure was the most impactful — the feature appeared to work (dashboard showed notifications) but the admin Telegram DM was silently failing because the backend could not find BOT_TOKEN in the Railway environment. This is a deployment hygiene issue: .env files are gitignored by design, so Railway must be explicitly configured with the same secrets. Going forward, I would add a startup check that logs clearly whether required environment variables are present, making silent failures like this immediately visible in Railway deployment logs.